From 6c88aaf7e78f3a5de3186138f65a59468efdfb11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sento Daimon <339524263+sentodaimon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:04:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Coin Series stage 3: per-block difficulty (ASERT anchored at
 height 1) with stall relief

- aserti3-2d integer evaluation, anchor = height 1 with parent time = genesis time,
  half-life 2 hours; pre-shift for RandomX-sized targets (> 2^224)
- stall relief: block more than 1 hour after its parent gets target x 2^((gap-3600)/1800),
  combined with the ASERT exponent; not applied at height 1; capped at powLimit
- per-chain future time limit (Coin Series: 10 minutes)
- placeholder start target for 1,000 H/s (600,000 hashes per block), limit = start x 4096
- miner updates difficulty when it updates the time; header sync accepts per-block changes
- regtest: -coinseriesasert enables the real rules (default fixed easiest difficulty)
- tests: anchor/height-2 vectors, half-life x2 / /2, relief x2 / x1024, 10-minute shift = 1.26x,
  limit cap, integer accuracy, 1000x inflow/exit simulation with the real function
